---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Integrated Campaign Management | Kelp Agency"
  description="Kelp plans and manages campaigns across message, creative, channels, landing pages, timing, and measurement."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Digital Marketing Services"
    title="Campaign Management"
    description="Campaigns break down when good ideas never turn into coordinated execution. We plan and manage campaigns so the message, timeline, assets, and budget all move in the same direction."
    lottieFile="campaign-management.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Campaign problems usually are not about a lack of ideas. They come from
        too many moving parts with no one keeping the strategy, timeline,
        creative, and budget aligned.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is when launch dates slip, content arrives late, spend gets wasted,
        and the campaign never builds the momentum it should.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We help define the campaign story, the rollout plan, the channel mix,
        and the production rhythm needed to support it. Then we manage the
        details so the work keeps moving after kickoff instead of stalling under
        its own weight.
      </p>
      <h2>From Idea to Operating Plan</h2>
      <p>
        We define who the campaign is for, what action it should produce, which
        proof the audience needs, and how the work will be delivered. The
        production plan covers assets, channels, owners, deadlines, tracking,
        and review points. That helps a team keep the campaign coherent when
        several people or vendors are involved.
      </p>
      <h2>Improve While the Campaign Is Running</h2>
      <p>
        We compare performance with the intended outcome, not only impressions
        or clicks. Creative, targeting, and the destination page can all be
        adjusted as evidence comes in. Kelp's <a href="/work/elev8-fun/">Elev8 Fun</a> work is an example of
        campaign, design, paid social, website, and support work moving
        together. Talk through your next campaign.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        A good launch plan identifies the owner of every asset and decision. We
        build in time for review, testing, and changes in the offer, rather than
        assuming the first version will be final. After launch, the team needs a
        shared view of spend, response, lead quality, and what customers are
        asking. Those observations guide the next creative or landing-page
        change.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Campaign brief and audience priorities</li>
        <li>Asset list with owners, approvals, and deadlines</li>
        <li>Channel and landing-page coordination</li>
        <li>Reporting cadence and post-campaign recommendations</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the launch date, business goal, known constraints, and team
        members who will approve the work. We can then recommend a realistic
        rollout and the production support it requires.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can Kelp work with our internal team?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. We can coordinate the full campaign or own the parts that need
        outside strategy, creative, development, or media support.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Campaign
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={78} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
